Protein-Rich Foods for Period Meals

Protein is an important part of a balanced diet. It supports normal body functions and helps make meals more satisfying. During your period, including protein in your meals can be a simple way to build a more balanced eating routine.

Eggs are an easy protein source. You can prepare boiled eggs, omelettes, scrambled eggs, or egg sandwiches. Add vegetables and whole-grain toast for a simple meal.

For vegetarian and vegan diets, lentils, chickpeas, beans, peas, tofu, soy products, nuts, and seeds can provide plant-based protein.

Dal is particularly easy to include in Indian meals. Pair it with rice, chapati, vegetables, or millet-based foods depending on your preference.

Chickpeas can be used in many different ways. You can make chana curry, chickpea salad, roasted chickpeas, or a chickpea wrap. Beans can similarly be used in curries, rice dishes, soups, and salads.

Tofu can be stir-fried with vegetables or added to curries and wraps. Paneer can also be included if you eat dairy products.

Yoghurt can provide protein and can be eaten with meals or used as a snack. Try adding fruit, oats, or seeds to yoghurt for a simple bowl.

Nuts and seeds are convenient snacks and can be added to oatmeal, salads, smoothies, and yoghurt. Because they are energy-dense, a small serving can be enough.

You can create balanced meals by combining protein with carbohydrates and vegetables. Examples include dal with rice and vegetables, eggs with toast and fruit, or chickpeas with chapati and salad.

There is no need to follow an extreme high-protein diet. Your nutritional needs depend on factors such as age, body size, activity, and overall health.

Regular meals, enough fluids, fruits, vegetables, and adequate rest can all form part of your period routine. If you experience severe or unusual menstrual symptoms, food should not replace professional medical advice.

Menstrual hygiene is another important consideration. Carrying spare sanitary pads can be especially useful if you spend long hours outside. Choose products based on comfort and your personal flow.

